            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0378" n="366" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg366"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.7962/57: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-10T09:00:00-00:44">March 10, 1942—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 10—8:31 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>64. From McBride. Colonel Fox, Captain Beard and I called on President Barclay
                    yesterday. He assured Fox of fullest cooperation in his investigation of health
                    conditions. Surveys of Fox and Beard in progress.</p>
                <p>Hope details of credit plan can be sent promptly as I must soon inform Barclay
                    thereof. [McBride.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
